Amazing! We see again use the single step instruction to step through the program, first we step the the mov ax, 1234h instruction and display it's memory, .XAX=1234- shows that AX does have 1234h stored in it. Then we skip to the last instruction before jmp stop and display the AX reg again. At this point if our program was correct, it should display the independently populated AH and AL as FFABh, and we see that is indeed does!

This shows that regs can be accessed and manipulated with the high byte and low byte independently.
